+# Rewards registration integration
+
+The static page implements three steps, accessible validation, review, and submission. It does not create accounts without a backend. Serve the site over HTTPS in production.
+
+Implement these same-origin endpoints:
+
+- `GET /api/rewards/csrf`: return JSON `{ "token": "..." }` with a cryptographically random, session-bound CSRF token. Use `Cache-Control: no-store` and a `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite` session cookie.
+- `POST /api/rewards/register`: accept JSON containing `givenName`, `familyName`, `email`, optional `birthday` (`YYYY-MM-DD` or null), `password`, `termsAccepted`, and `marketingOptIn`. Validate the `X-CSRF-Token` header against the session and check the request origin. Return a successful JSON response `{ "created": true }` only after account creation. Other responses display a generic, retryable error; no server text is inserted into HTML.
+
+The server must independently validate field lengths, email format, birthday validity, password length (15–128 characters), and required terms acceptance. Store consent records and honor the separate, default-off marketing choice. Apply rate limits, verify email ownership, avoid account enumeration, and hash passwords using a suitable password-hashing algorithm such as Argon2id. Do not log passwords, CSRF tokens, or request bodies. Set appropriate security headers, including a CSP covering the page's Google Fonts and Unsplash image dependencies.
+
+No credentials or personal information are written to browser storage or URL parameters. Data stays in form memory for retry and is cleared after confirmed success. The client requests a CSRF token before transmitting registration data, rejects unexpected content types and redirects on account submission, disables repeat submissions, and times out requests after 15 seconds. A static host without the API shows the unavailable-service error and never reports a successful signup.
+
+For production, link `/terms`, `/privacy-policy`, and `/account` to the corresponding real pages, and make program benefit copy consistent with the final rewards terms.
